  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "For a real number \\(x,\\) define \\(\\heartsuit(x)\\) to be the average of \\(x\\) and \\(x^2.\\) What is the value of the following expression? \\[\\heartsuit(1)+\\heartsuit(2)+\\heartsuit(3)\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(12\\)",
    "E": "\\(20\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The average of two numbers is their sum divided by \\(2\\), so the definition gives \\(\\heartsuit(x)=(x+x^2)/2\\). Substituting the three inputs,\n\\[\n\\heartsuit(1)=\\frac{1+1}{2}=1,\n\\qquad\n\\heartsuit(2)=\\frac{2+4}{2}=3,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\heartsuit(3)=\\frac{3+9}{2}=6.\n\\]\nTheir sum is \\(1+3+6=\\boxed{10}\\), choice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
